    "title": "4 send to hospital with carbon monoxide poisoning in Bucks County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tom Dougherty Ben Payne ,\n2 hours ago\n4 hospitalized with carbon monoxide poisoning in Lower Southampton, Bucks County 00:24\nFour people were hospitalized with carbon monoxide poisoning in Lower Southampton, Pennsylvania, according to Bucks County dispatch.\nBucks County dispatch told CBS News Philadelphia that first responders responded to a home in the 300 block of Philmont Avenue just after 8 p.m. Thursday.\nFour victims were rushed to the hospital, Bucks County dispatch said. They said three dogs and a canary were also affected. The township said all four people were conscious, but didn't have an update on their conditions.\nThe source of the carbon monoxide remains under investigation.",
    "summary": "By Tom Dougherty Ben Payne , 4 hospitalized with carbon monoxide poisoning in Lower Southampton, Bucks County 00:24 Four people were hospitalized with carbon monoxide poisoning in Lower Southampton, Pennsylvania, according to Bucks County dispatch. Bucks County dispatch told CBS News Philadelphia that first responders responded to a home in the 300 block of Philmont Avenue just after 8 p.m. Thursday. Four victims were rushed to the hospital, Bucks County dispatch said. The township said all four people were conscious, but didn't have an update on their conditions. The source of the carbon monoxide remains under investigation.",
